<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mérida, Yucatán</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mérida is the capital of the Mexican state of Yucatán. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-de-montejo-the-younger">Francisco de Montejo the Younger</a> founded it in 1542 on the site of the Maya city of T'hó, reusing stone from its pyramids. It was the seat of the Spanish province of Yucatán and of the breakaway Republic of Yucatán in the 1840s, and grew rich on henequen fibre in the late 19th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/merida-yucatan.jpg" alt="Mérida, Yucatán" width="320" height="533" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: the above mentioned · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Collage_Merida_Yucatan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
